From: conda-forge/graphblas-feedstock
Subject: [PATCH] Declare OpenMP loop variable outside the for statement in
 GB_I_inverse

MSVC only implements OpenMP 2.0, which requires the loop iteration
variable of an `omp for` construct to be declared before the loop
rather than in the init clause. Otherwise the build fails with:

    Source\extract\GB_I_inverse.c(85): error C3015: initialization in
    OpenMP 'for' statement has improper form

The loop variable of an `omp for` is predetermined private, so hoisting
the declaration out of the loop does not change behavior.

diff --git a/Source/extract/GB_I_inverse.c b/Source/extract/GB_I_inverse.c
index f281b27ae1..7e8e33027a 100644
--- a/Source/extract/GB_I_inverse.c
+++ b/Source/extract/GB_I_inverse.c
@@ -81,8 +81,9 @@ GrB_Info GB_I_inverse           // invert the I list for C=A(I,:)
     int nthreads = GB_nthreads (nI, chunk, nthreads_max) ;
 
     GB_IPTR (W, W_is_32) ;
+    int64_t k ;
     #pragma omp parallel for num_threads(nthreads) schedule(static)
-    for (int64_t k = 0 ; k < nI ; k++)
+    for (k = 0 ; k < nI ; k++)
     { 
         // W [k] = k
         GB_ISET (W, k, k) ;
